title: Start
---
<<declare $quest = "Read note">>
<<declare $Items = "">>

Narrator: You wake up after a long nights rest
Narrator: You remember there was something you had to do. Just not what
Narrator: you see a note on the table 

===
title: note
---
The note: reminder to self: go pick flowers tomorrow
Narrator: you decide to head out and go pick some flowers on the field to the left of your house
<<set $quest = "Go to the flower field">>
===
title: CometCrash
---

Narrator: You see a comet falling down the sky and decide to check it out
Narrator: the comet is to the right of the flower field
<<set $quest = "Check out the crash">>
===

title: seeAlien
---
<<set $quest = "Talk to Alien">>
===
title: TalkToAlien
---
<<if $quest == "Talk to Alien">>
    Alien: GDKKN GTLZM
    Alien: *Rebooting Language system*
    Alien: Sorry, Hello Human!
    Alien: My ship seems to have crashed near you, i apologise for the mess it has caused.
    Alien: It had a leak in the fluecent lucid, some of it may have spilled into the nearby area.
    Alien: *Scanning for injuries*
    Alien: You seem to be unharmed, my system does pickup something quite unusual.
    Alien: It seems like the leakage had some effect on you, can you try and focus on this stone behind me?
    Alien: Imagine it floating, then grab the ship's blueprint tabloid from underneath it.
<<set $quest to "grab blueprint">>

<<elseif $quest == "grab blueprint">>
    
    Alien: Welcome back human, did you grab my blueprint from underneath the stone behind me??

<<elseif $quest == "Report back to Alien">>
    <<if has_item("Player", "bluePrint")>>
        Alien: Thank you human, now we can find out what we need to repair my ship.
        Alien: My database shows that some ship parts landed in the nearby area.
        Alien: Can you grab those while I work on getting the fluecent lucid tank working again?
        Alien: Also Human, the parts of my ship will look like what you call Crystals
        <<set $quest to "find Parts">>
        <<set $Items = "2/2 remaining">>
        

    <<else>>
        Alien: I need the blueprint from underneath that stone right there.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $quest == "find Parts">>
    
    Alien: Did you find the missing parts I asked you to find?

    <<if has_item("Player", "clinkClank")>>
    Alien: Good job on finding the first part! I will repair my ship further.
    Alien: can you find this part aswell? I circled it on the blueprint again.

    <<else>>
    Alien: I'm almost finished fixing the fluecent lucid tank.
    Alien: Please grab the remaining parts so that we can put my ship back together.

    <<endif>>

<<elseif $quest == "Return to Alien">>    

    <<if has_item ("Player", "desicleDemo")>>
    
    Alien: Thank you for helping me find the parts for my ship human!
    <<set_enabled_in_unity "GameMusic" false>> 
    <<set_enabled_in_unity "EnemySound" true>>
    <<play_animation "CuteAlien" "AlienBad" false>>
    <<play_animation "Crashed Ship" "MadRock" false>>
    
    Alien: I will now be off to destroy humanity!
    Alien: I hope you have a nice day, since it will be your last

    Narrator: Congratulations player, this is the end of the game
    Narrator: Sadly for you, this is the bad ending
    Narrator: Feel free to play again and try to find the good ending :D

    <<set $quest = "End of game,  Bad Ending unlocked">>
    
    <<else>>
    Alien: I'm almost finished fixing the fluecent lucid tank.
    Alien: Please grab the remaining parts so that we can put my ship back together.

    
<<endif>>

<<elseif $quest == "Return to Alien with Fox">>

    Alien: Thank you for helping me find the parts for my ship human!

    <<set_enabled_in_unity "GameMusic" false>> 
    <<set_enabled_in_unity "EnemySound" true>>
    <<play_animation "CuteAlien" "AlienBad" false>>
    <<play_animation "Crashed Ship" "MadRock" false>>
    
    Alien: I will now be off to destroy humanity!
    Alien: I hope you have a nice day, since it will be your last

    Fox: No! that' s MY human.
    Fox: They are kind and amazing.
    Fox: I won' t let you get away with this!

    Narrator: You see the Fox attacking the Alien
    Narrator: the Fox somehow beat the Alien and saved the world
    <<play_animation "CuteAlien" "AlienPoof" false>>
    <<set_enabled_in_unity "GameMusic" true>>
    <<set_enabled_in_unity "EnemySound" false>> 

    Narrator: Congratulations player

    <<set $quest = "End of game, congratulations good ending unlocked">>

<<endif>>

===
title: TalkToFox
---
Please don't hurt me
*You realize you can hear the fox tlaking somehow*
-> Be kind to the fox
    <<jump FoxKind>>
-> Leave the fox
    Narrator: you leave the fox alone in the cave
    <<stop>>
-> Be mean to the fox
    Narrator: You are mean to the fox
    Narrator: You see the fox running away as you feel like a terrible human being
    
    //play an animation of the fox running away while you hear cries
===


title: FoxKind
---
You: I won't hurt you no worries
    Fox: Wait- you can hear me?
    You: It appears so..?
    You: What is a small fox like you even doing in a cave?
    Fox: I got scared from the loud noise outside so i hid in this cave.
    Fox: Can i go with you? You seem like a nice person!
    ->Ofcourse!
        Narrator: The fox will now follow you!
        <<if has_item ("Player", "clinkClank")>>
            <<set $quest = "Find last part with Fox">>
        <<elseif has_item ("Player", "desicleDemo")>>
            <<set $quest = "Return to Alien With Fox">>
        <<else>>
            <<set $quest = "Find parts with fox">>
        <<endif>>  
    ->No.
        Narrator: The fox stays in the cave, scared and confused thinking you don't like him.
===

title: wrongStone
---
Alien: That is my ship human, please do not try to move it
